282
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,980
I've received a report.

283
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:06,860
Not just the chief's office,

284
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,080
you ran riot all over the place, I hear.

285
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,380
Well, that was...

286
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,640
because those guys'
attitude was just too awful,

287
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,200
so I just...

288
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:15,320
YOU IDIOTS!

289
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:18,460
You, who lead the most
carefree life in all of Japan,

290
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,780
have no right to comment
on other people's attitudes.

291
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:22,700
Honestly,
you have no sense of your own place.

292
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,720
Anyway,
for the trouble you caused this shop,

293
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,880
I'm deducting it from your salary,
understand?

294
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:28,560
That's too much!

295
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,380
If you dock my pay on
top of working for free,

296
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:34,060
what's the point of working at all?

297
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:37,480
Then mend your ways and work honestly!

298
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,680
Come on, apologize, Ryotsu!

299
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,580
That hurts, Chief!

300
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,920
Now, now, Mr. Ohara,
there's no need to go this far.

301
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:47,220
If he causes any more trouble,
please let us know.

302
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:51,540
Understood. Since this time
you're the one who recommended him,

303
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,300
we could really use any
extra hands right now.

304
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:55,880
Thank you, we appreciate it.

305
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:18,800
Ugh, Chief,
you'll pay for making us work for free!

306
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:21,060
Okay, six of the upper halves are done.

307
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:24,760
So why do I have to tag along too?

308
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:25,664
Now, now,

309
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:30,320
don't be so stiff. Let's share the joy of labor together,
shall we?

310
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,360
Come on, while you're still young.

311
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:36,780
I had a bad feeling from the
moment my senpai called me out.

312
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:42,720
This place is actually pretty good.

313
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:44,440
Let's go!

314
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:45,240
Come on! Go!

315
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:45,740
Whoa!

316
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,160
Manager, please come to the
reception room immediately.

317
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,060
Chief Ohara from Katsushika
Police Station is here.

318
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,240
What?

319
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:57,940
A welcome reception for overseas guests,
here at our station?

320
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,780
Yes. They suddenly decided to
come for an inspection tomorrow,

321
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,760
I know it's an unreasonable request,

322
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:08,120
but we were hoping very
much to use this place.

323
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:08,480
I see.

324
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,080
Isn't this about me?

325
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:13,840
It's a request from none
other than Mr. Ohara.

326
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:15,320
Let's see what we can do.

327
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:16,140
Well then,

328
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:18,820
leave it to us.

329
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:19,840
Thank you very much.

330
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:26,180
This is our chance for revenge.

331
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:30,420
What? All the cooks are off?

332
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,720
Yes, we just got a call.

333
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:35,600
They suddenly fell ill and said
they'd be taking the day off.

334
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,120
Good grief.

335
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:40,140
And today's the welcome reception
at Katsushika Police Station!

336
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:45,680
Shoddy construction was found in the restaurant building,
so we're closing temporarily tomorrow.

337
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,720
There's no need to worry.

338
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:56,080
Actually, I know someone very close to me
who once served as head chef at a famous hotel.

339
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,000
Really?

340
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:01,800
What's more, he once beat those
Iron Chefs in a cooking battle.

341
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,300
No way!

342
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:07,940
He's put down his knife for certain reasons right now,
but if I ask him, I'm sure he'll rush right over.

343
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:12,280
Please, call that person right away.

344
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:14,980
Understood, leave it to me.

345
00:18:14,980 --> 00:18:19,680
But that person really hates
being watched while he cooks.

346
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:24,400
Even the manager must never
peek into the kitchen, please.

347
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:28,500
Understood, I swear I won't peek.

348
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:31,740
He's late, isn't he?
That chef your senpai knows.

349
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:33,920
There's no way a guy
like that exists, idiot.

350
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:37,340
Then what about today's food?

351
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,740
I'll make it myself!

352
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,327
As a token of our everyday gratitude,

353
00:18:42,377 --> 00:18:47,040
the chiefs will get to savor the Ryotsu-style
special menu to their hearts' content.

354
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:49,880
Right then, let's get started!

355
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:53,174
The basics of cooking are soup, after all.

356
00:18:53,224 --> 00:18:56,680
First, let's get plenty of
dashi stock from my own body.

357
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:01,130
We were allowed to
observe the Japanese police,

358
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:03,600
and it was a very meaningful day.

359
00:19:03,650 --> 00:19:06,500
I would like to express my gratitude here.

360
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:09,440
Thank you very much, Minister Gomez.

361
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:11,640
What is he saying?

362
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:14,180
It was very meaningful. He says thank you.

363
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:17,260
Thank you. Thank you, please.

364
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,400
Thank you very much, have a nice day.

365
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:26,520
Minister, shall we now have our meal?

366
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:27,920
Right.

367
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:38,180
Looks like you're being serious about this.

368
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:38,760
Of course.

369
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,580
This is our restaurant's special menu.

370
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:47,520
This restaurant has first-class chefs.

371
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,620
Please try this delicacy
you rarely get to taste.

372
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,700
Please eat it before it gets cold.

373
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:54,980
Well then, shall we dig in?

374
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,200
What kind of soup is this?

375
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,500
Ryo-chan, what kind of soup is this?

376
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,380
It's aojiru, the green juice that's all the rage right now,
prepared with French cooking techniques.

377
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:09,980
I turned it into a soup with a unique,
rich flavor.

378
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:12,240
The chef said it's his masterpiece.

379
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,080
Next dish.

380
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,680
I love sushi!

381
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,940
There's chocolate inside, isn't there?

382
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,840
A traditional Japanese dish.

383
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:36,840
It's said to be a fusion of
sushi and Western confectionery.

384
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,660
The after-meal drink is cocoa.

385
00:20:40,460 --> 00:20:43,060
Please enjoy this blend of
Japanese and Western flavors.

386
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,380
They're eating it, they're eating it.

387
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:47,160
Everyone's eating it so well

388
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:51,020
It's because people assume a
top-class chef made it, right.

389
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:53,280
Human tongues are really unreliable,
aren't they.

390
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:56,120
Right, let's prepare the next dish!

391
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,440
Tempura!

392
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:03,500
It's tempura garnished with
jelly gummies and natatecoco.

393
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:05,880
Please enjoy the unique texture.

394
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:09,160
Please, Chief and Section Chief,
do try some.

395
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:11,660
Mm... well, truly, I can't say anything.

396
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,720
It's a spicy steak.

397
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:17,700
More like super-hot than spicy,
judging by looks alone.

398
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,960
A-are you all right, Ohara?

399
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,780
Whoa, excuse me for a moment.

400
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:36,860
Chief Ohara, how is it?
Are you enjoying yourself?

401
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:42,860
These dishes are wonderfully original.
I'm simply amazed.

402
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:44,460
I'm glad you're pleased.

403
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:51,000
Since the chef is an acquaintance of Ryotsu's,
I haven't eaten any of this myself.

404
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,620
What?

405
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:57,280
Actually, all of our chefs took
the day off in nine seconds.

406
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,160
Is something wrong?

407
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,720
Ryotsu, you...

408
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:06,960
For dessert, it's a firework cake!

409
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:09,820
A bold flavor that bursts in your mouth,
how about that?

410
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:12,460
Then you spread plenty
of cream all around it...

411
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:14,740
And this is a cake I made with such care!

412
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:16,620
With a fuse that doesn't
produce any smoke...

413
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:20,640
Just imagining what will
happen makes me excited.

414
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:21,980
I see.

415
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:24,300
Yo-chū!

416
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:27,000
Yes, Chief!

417
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,620
I knew it was you!

418
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:29,460
Chief!

419
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:41,760
What do we do, what do we do?

420
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:43,700
Whoa, what is that?

421
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:44,840
Whoa!

422
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:46,540
Whoa!

423
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:48,660
Do you really have to go that far?

424
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:51,300
Chief, it's just a bit of entertainment,
just a bit of entertainment!

425
00:22:51,300 --> 00:22:52,520
Whoa!

426
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:52,740
Whoa!

427
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:53,240
Aaaaaah!

428
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:57,340
Yeah, this way, this way!

429
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,620
Don't panic, the fire extinguisher!

430
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:00,440
Yes, here!

431
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,300
Right, first, the gas main valve!

432
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:05,860
Y-yes!

433
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:17,380
Chief, look! It came off!

434
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,260
Heh heh heh.

435
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:22,240
Aaaaaah!

436
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,060
Aaaaaah!

437
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:23,620
Aaaaaah!

438
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:32,860
Whew...

439
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:38,320
Chief, I'm glad you're unharmed, but please stop with the "you wretch" routine.
Chief, mistakes...

440
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:41,940
...happen to everyone,
but your very existence is a mistake!

441
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:45,020
Just as I thought, it's come to this.

442
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:46,280
What kind of chief...

443
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:49,280
You went to the trouble of introducing me,
after all.

444
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,580
Please, don't say another word.

445
00:23:50,580 --> 00:23:53,080
I understand perfectly
what you're trying to say.

446
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,460
Ryotsu, you...

447
00:23:55,460 --> 00:23:57,260
Chief, please stop.

448
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:58,640
I didn't do it on purpose, honest.

449
00:23:58,640 --> 00:23:59,540
Thanks for saving me.

450
00:24:03,340 --> 00:24:04,980
The bell of Enji

451
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:06,920
rings from inside a bottle, gong.

452
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:08,720
The room lights

453
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:10,360
fade out with a whoosh.

454
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:12,560
Curses!

455
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:14,840
Ghosts these days?

456
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:16,140
Nobody believes in that stuff, right?

457
00:24:16,140 --> 00:24:18,820
But don't you want to see a real ghost,
just once?

458
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:21,060
Next time: making a killing off ghosts!

459
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:21,860
See you then!

460
00:24:31,140 --> 00:24:34,680
Called a woman who can't fall in love,

461
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:37,040
though the rumors say so,

462
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:40,160
there are so many things

463
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,940
I want to do, piles upon piles.

464
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:42,700
Me,

465
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:52,040
I want to ride a motorbike
across a harsh desert.

466
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:59,260
I want to be freer than the birds.

467
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,200
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

